Phase 5 – Databricks + Olist End-to-End Data Engineering Pipeline
Overview

This project demonstrates an end-to-end data engineering pipeline using the Olist Brazilian E-commerce dataset in Databricks. The pipeline includes data ingestion, validation, transformation, modeling, advanced analytics using PySpark, and final reporting.

Objective
Work with a real-world multi-table dataset
Perform data ingestion and validation
Apply joins and aggregations
Use window functions for advanced analytics
Build a final reporting dataset
Dataset

Source: Kaggle – Olist Brazilian E-commerce Dataset
Format: CSV files

Tables used:

orders
customers
order_items
products
payments
Tools and Technologies
Databricks (Community Edition)
PySpark
SQL concepts (joins, aggregations, window functions)
Project Workflow
1. Data Ingestion
Uploaded all CSV files into Databricks
Loaded data using PySpark DataFrames
2. Data Validation
Checked schema and null values
Ensured correct joins using key columns
3. Data Modeling
Fact Tables: order_items, payments
Dimension Tables: customers, orders, products
4. Data Transformation
Joined multiple tables
Performed aggregations to derive insights
5. Advanced Analytics
Applied window functions:
row_number() for ranking
dense_rank() for category-based ranking
cumulative sum for running totals
6. Final Reporting

Created a consolidated dataset containing:

customer_id
customer_city
total_spend
segment
total_orders
Analytical Tasks
Task 1: Top 3 Customers per City

Calculated total spend per customer and used a window function to rank customers within each city.

Task 2: Running Total of Sales

Computed daily sales and applied a cumulative sum to calculate running totals.

Task 3: Top Products per Category

Aggregated product-level sales and ranked them within each category using dense_rank().

Task 4: Customer Lifetime Value (CLV)

Calculated total spend per customer across all orders.

Task 5: Customer Segmentation

Segmented customers based on total spend:

Gold: total_spend > 10000
Silver: total_spend between 5000 and 10000
Bronze: total_spend < 5000
Task 6: Final Reporting Table

Combined all processed data into a single dataset for reporting and analysis.